questions.question:
The first version of the retry queue stored the update that failed:

// on failure
retryQueue.push({ userId, total });
// drainer, every 5 s while the breaker allows calls
const { userId, total } = retryQueue[0];
await redis.zadd("leaderboard", total, userId);

Log for one learner:
10:00:01.120 u_51 total=120 ZADD failed (timeout) -> queued { u_51, 120 }
10:00:40.002 redis recovered, leaderboard breaker half-open -> closed
10:00:41.310 u_51 total=150 ZADD ok
10:00:45.000 drain ZADD leaderboard 120 u_51 ok

Statement: "ZADD with an absolute score is idempotent, so replaying the queued update after recovery is safe and the leaderboard ends with 150 for u_51."
